# Explicit line-ending declarations for files this PR touches or that are
# structurally risky to diff as plain text. Deliberately NOT a blanket
# `* text=auto` policy: an audit while preparing this PR found 13 other
# pre-existing files across the repo (.gitignore, several *.rs sources,
# mc-bot/package.json, two docs) already carrying CRLF line endings while the
# rest of the repo is LF. Renormalizing those is a legitimate but separate
# cleanup with its own review surface -- out of scope here, and not something
# this PR should decide unilaterally by dropping a repo-wide attribute.
#
# CHANGELOG.md: declared explicitly because it was accidentally flattened
# from CRLF to LF by a Python text-mode read/write round-trip while preparing
# this PR (Python's universal-newlines translation strips \r on read; the
# write side does not restore it on Linux). That turned a ~40-line content
# edit into a ~2000-line diff.
#
# `-text` (not `text eol=crlf`): the `text` attribute always normalizes the
# STORED blob to LF regardless of `eol=`, which only controls what gets
# materialized on checkout -- so `text eol=crlf` would silently re-flatten
# this file to LF in the repository on every commit while merely rendering it
# as CRLF locally, reproducing the exact bug this line exists to prevent.
# `-text` (without `-diff`): opts the path out of EOL processing entirely
# -- git stores and checks out exactly the bytes on disk, in either
# direction -- while still generating a normal line-based diff (unlike
# Cargo.lock/*.wasm below, a CHANGELOG is meant to be read in review).
CHANGELOG.md -text

# Lockfiles and generated binaries: never text-diff or line-ending-convert.
# A regenerated lockfile is reviewed by its dependency delta, not a
# line-by-line text diff, and a wasm-pack .wasm binary must never have EOL
# translation applied (which would corrupt it on a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf enabled).
Cargo.lock -text -diff
package-lock.json -text -diff
*.wasm -text -diff binary
